# UI Guard Rules

When the task involves UI (screens, components, layout, navigation, panels, dialogs):

1. Locate or create a wireframe under `wireframes/` before writing implementation code.
2. Ensure the wireframe contains clear acceptance criteria (Goal/Screen + Acceptance).
3. After implementing, run or request an adversarial review against those criteria.
4. Do not consider the UI change complete until the review verdict is PASS or an accepted PASS WITH NOTES.
5. Prefer separate builder and critic roles — do not self-approve your own UI work.
6. Update visual baselines only after intentional visual changes are approved.

See the `ui-standards` and `ui-require-wireframe` skills for the full contract.
